Add a skipBlockSignatureValidation flag.

Differential testing runs every client with validate_result = false: the block
signature and the post-state root go unchecked while RANDAO, attestation and
the other BLS checks stay on. Nimbus's existing skipBlsValidation is all or
nothing, so a client running under it accepts blocks with a bad RANDAO reveal
and stops disagreeing with pyspec exactly where this project wants it to.

The new flag sits beside skipBlsValidation in UpdateFlag and is honoured at the
one place that verifies the proposer's signature. Nothing else reads it, so
skipBlsValidation keeps its current meaning.
diff --git a/beacon_chain/extras.nim b/beacon_chain/extras.nim
index 66c479e..15dde30 100644
--- a/beacon_chain/extras.nim
+++ b/beacon_chain/extras.nim
@@ -24,6 +24,9 @@ type
     ## Skip verification of BLS signatures in block processing.
     ## Predominantly intended for use in testing, e.g. to allow extra coverage.
     ## Also useful to avoid unnecessary work when replaying known, good blocks.
+    skipBlockSignatureValidation ##\
+    ## Skip verification of block proposer signature only.
+    ## Unlike skipBlsValidation, this does not disable other BLS checks.
     skipStateRootValidation ##\
     ## Skip verification of block state root.
     strictVerification ##\
diff --git a/beacon_chain/spec/state_transition.nim b/beacon_chain/spec/state_transition.nim
index d53a0f6..b3f07b0 100644
--- a/beacon_chain/spec/state_transition.nim
+++ b/beacon_chain/spec/state_transition.nim
@@ -253,7 +253,7 @@ proc state_transition_block_aux(
   # by the block proposer. Every actor in the network will update its state
   # according to the contents of this block - but first they will validate
   # that the block is sane.
-  if skipBlsValidation notin flags:
+  if skipBlsValidation notin flags and skipBlockSignatureValidation notin flags:
     ? verify_block_signature(state.data, signedBlock)
 
   trace "state_transition: processing block, signature passed",
